('dabfd28b-8b1f-51b3-86df-2ec1bd6e883f'::uuid,'est','"Solid Geometry & Volume"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"The volume of a cube is given by the formula s³, where s is the length of a side. If a cube has a volume of 64, and the length of each side is halved, the new cube''s volume will be:"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"3"},{"key":"G","text":"6"},{"key":"H","text":"8"},{"key":"J","text":"16"},{"key":"K","text":"32"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-48","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Solid Geometry & Volume"}'::jsonb,'"H"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-48)."'::jsonb),
('15d4b0bf-4abf-53bd-bfa7-9daeda66b574'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"In the parallelogram below, lengths are given in inches. What is the area of the parallelogram, in square inches?\n[Figure: Parallelogram with top and bottom sides 7; slant sides √47; overall height 9 indicated by a vertical bracket on the left.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"√94"},{"key":"B","text":"7√47"},{"key":"C","text":"49"},{"key":"D","text":"63"},{"key":"E","text":"16√47"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"pt2.md","source_sha256":"dc3f96cb13caae485d8f8df3913a14000c0cee73962cf2be70e8202d99a231b9","source_question_id":"P2-49","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations","image":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/xxx64220-debug/ghoneem-math-portal/main/assets/question-bank/P2-49.png","image_alt":"Original graph, diagram, or table for P2-49","visual_verified":true}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from pt2.md (P2-49)."'::jsonb),
